                        "recommendationid": "237454798",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198041147604",
                            "num_reviews": 5,
                            "playtime_forever": 1277,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 926,
                            "last_played": 1791786092
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is fantastic.  One of the best horror games i've played.  Atmosphere and tension are amazing, and make the build up to the scares so good.  The game is so smart it actually makes you scare yourself more often than not.  A lot of the negative reviews are quite honestly from people that needed extra time on tests in school, that want their hands held and cant figure things out for themselves.  This game respects the player's intelligence, and lets you freely explore and figure things out for yourself.  Once you DO actually figure things out its incredibly satisfying and rewarding.  One negative review literally said \"the puzzles are confusing\" and that they couldnt find answers with chatGPT and Gemini.  We are literally living through the death of intellect.  \n\nIf you like horror, play Visage.  It's worth every penny.",
